          "mainline": "mathematics",
          "refutation_inputs": [],
          "statement": "At every finite-interior n=2 symmetric INF branch point with R>1 in the exact M3 contract, the normalized odd-sector matrix M=[[a0-gamma1,b0],[b0,b0-gamma2]] has b0>0 and gamma2>b0, so its lower-right entry is strictly negative and det M>0 is equivalent to S_KP=a0-gamma1+b0^2/(gamma2-b0)<0. Under the exact five-phase spectral, band, mass, and mode-index system of the proof package, S_KP<0 is equivalent to the explicit elementary inequality Phi<0 and equality is equivalent to Phi=0. Any same-sign kernel obeys the common projective-flux identity, has a unique simple downward locking point in the stated interval, and has positive endpoint impulse ratio (gamma2-b0)/b0. These are exact reductions only: the sign of Phi, det Kp_odd>0 for all finite-interior points, KO-DET, and global G1-prime remain open.",
